## The constitution is laid ({{EDITION}})

This repository gained its AI layer today: `docs/ai/` at edition **{{EDITION}}**,
the OKF bundle, the case and journal homes, the changelog, and the entry document
the agents read. The stacks this repository subscribes to: {{STACK_SUMMARY}}.

**Why this entry exists rather than an empty journal.** The scaffold commits
files outside `docs/`, and the audit's `journal-recency` check reads exactly
that — work touched, no day recorded. A repository that fails its own audit on
the day it is created gives the wrong first impression of the artifact whose
whole purpose is that the repository's law is trustworthy
(`sy11a/Architector#364`). So the scaffold records its own act, which is true
rather than filler, and the ritual starts with a real entry instead of a rule
nobody has yet obeyed.

**What is not decided yet, and belongs in the next entries.** This repository has
verification bindings that name no gate beyond `legislator anchors`, no ADR but
the one recording that ADRs are kept, and no case. The first real day of
work is where those begin; `docs/ai/rules/core/dev-journal.md` says what an entry
carries — dead ends, open questions, decisions with their reasoning — and none of
those exist yet, which is the honest content of a scaffold day.
